{"name":"Sea Quest","hex":"#3e7984","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Semai."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large body of salt water.","The ocean; the continuous body of salt water covering a majority of the Earth's surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea"},{"term":"quest","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A journey or effort in pursuit of a goal (often lengthy, ambitious, or fervent); a mission.","A task that a player may complete in order to gain a reward or advance the story."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To seek or pursue a goal; to undertake a mission or job.","To search for something; to seek."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quest"}],"entries":[{"title":"SeaQuest (aquariums)","blocks":[{"text":"SeaQuest Holdings, LLC better known as just SeaQuest, was an interactive marine, exotic mammal, and bird/reptile life attraction chain. It was founded by Vince Covino and featured hands-on animal interactions at shopping malls throughout the United States. The company has no locations. SeaQuest has attracted considerable controversy and legal issues due to concerns over its animal care standards."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/66/SeaQuest_logo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SeaQuest_(aquariums)"},{"title":"SeaQuest DSV (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"seaQuest DSV is an action/strategy video game depiction of the seaQuest DSV television series for developed by Sculptured Software. A Super Nintendo Entertainment System version was published in 1994 and a Sega Genesis port in 1995. The player captains the submarine seaQuest DSV 4600 to carry out a series of missions in a scrolling, underwater environment."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/78/Seaquestdsvsnes.jpg/330px-Seaquestdsvsnes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SeaQuest_DSV_(video_game)"},{"title":"Sea Quest (drilling rig)","blocks":[{"text":"The Sea Quest was a semi-submersible drilling rig. She discovered the UK's first North Sea oil on 14 September 1969 in the Arbroath Field. She also discovered the first giant oil field named Forties on 7 October 1970."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_Quest_(drilling_rig)"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/SeaQuest_tegu.jpg/500px-SeaQuest_tegu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/SeaQuest_tegu.jpg/500px-SeaQuest_tegu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"SeaQuest employee with an Asian water monitor","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASeaQuest_tegu.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/SeaQuest_mermaid.jpg/500px-SeaQuest_mermaid.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/SeaQuest_mermaid.jpg/1280px-SeaQuest_mermaid.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/SeaQuest_mermaid.jpg/500px-SeaQuest_mermaid.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"SeaQuest employee dressed as a mermaid","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASeaQuest_mermaid.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/SeaQuest_Boy_with_snake.jpg/500px-SeaQuest_Boy_with_snake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/SeaQuest_Boy_with_snake.jpg/500px-SeaQuest_Boy_with_snake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A kid petting a snake at SeaQuest","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASeaQuest_Boy_with_snake.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/05/SeaQuest_DSV_SNES_Concept_designs.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/05/SeaQuest_DSV_SNES_Concept_designs.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"The various designs from oldest (left) to newest (right) as used in the game","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASeaQuest_DSV_SNES_Concept_designs.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/BlueMarble-2001-2002.jpg/500px-BlueMarble-2001-2002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/BlueMarble-2001-2002.jpg/1280px-BlueMarble-2001-2002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/BlueMarble-2001-2002.jpg/500px-BlueMarble-2001-2002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Composite images of the Earth created by NASA in 2001","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlueMarble-2001-2002.j